adyToRead\"\n        ],\n        \"contexts\": [\n          \"One stable leader term with committed current-term entry and fixed full-voter membership\",\n          \"Distinct concurrent SystemCtx values, later context confirmed before earlier context\"\n        ],\n        \"event_paths\": [\n          \"Peer.ReadIndex -> follower forwarding -> leader readIndex.addRequest -> voter HeartbeatResp -> confirm prefix -> forwarded response -> follower ReadyToRead\"\n        ],\n        \"activity_classes\": [\n          \"A2\"\n        ],\n        \"behavior_ids\": [\n          \"B-read-confirm\",\n          \"B-read-route\"\n        ],\n        \"fact_ids\": [\n          \"F-read-release\"\n        ],\n        \"supporting_behavior_ids\": {\n          \"B-authority\": \"Term establishment/reset and filtering qualify same-term confirmation.\",\n          \"B-replicate\": \"Current-term committed entry is the multi-voter read admission condition.\",\n          \"B-client-read\": \"Actual consumer uses exact context keys and separates readiness from timeout.\",\n          \"B-persist\": \"Update processing orders durable messages; a driver must honor this when using Peer.\"\n        },\n        \"obligation_relation_kind\": \"consumption\",\n        \"counterevidence\": [\n          \"Local completion correctly uses s.ctx; nonzero context probes go only to voters.\",\n          \"A later confirmation legitimately covers earlier read boundaries and raises their index; index equality to the original captured commit would be an overstrong oracle.\",\n          \"Client API allows timeout/drop and therefore supplies no unconditional eventual-success deadline.\"\n        ],\n        \"unknowns\": [\n          \"Actual same-history response/readiness contexts under a legal overlap remain unmeasured.\"\n        ],\n        \"priority\": 2,\n        \"trigger_rationale\": \"readIndex.confirm returns original per-status contexts, local completion uses s.ctx, but remote reply uses the single triggering m.Hint/m.HintHigh. Receiver and client match the returned context exactly. This concrete source difference makes a small controlled overlap test informative; another source-only guard search cannot establish its actual routed output.\"\n      },\n      \"status\": \"escalated\",\n      \"parent_candidate_id\": null,\n      \"fork_reason\": \"\",\n      \"stop_reason\": \"Ground the selected status-consumption responsibility without assuming a violation or any unconditional client deadline.\",\n      \"resume_conditions\": [],\n      \"obligation_id\": \"C-forwarded-context\",\n      \"result_claim_ids\": [\n        \"C-forwarded-context\"\n      ],\n      \"open_issue_ids\": [],\n      \"executions\": [\n        {\n          \"check_id\": \"957fd78098304be69986dc2a90daee5c\",\n          \"artifact_id\": \"b21be9de584f4ca6b5964cbf24384304\",\n          \"action\": \"direct_check\",\n          \"status\": \"completed\",\n          \"outcome\": \"tests_failed\",\n          \"record\": {\n            \"path\": \"state.json\",\n            \"collection\": \"checks\",\n            \"match\": {\n              \"id\": \"957fd78098304be69986dc2a90daee5c\"\n            }\n          }\n        }\n      ],\n      \"record\": {\n        \"path\": \"state.json\",\n        \"collection\": \"question_candidates\",\n        \"match\": {\n          \"id\": \"5c6bc6e6b4484bef902a59f3fa66e33b\"\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"units\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"unit-C-forwarded-context\",\n      \"candidate_id\": \"5c6bc6e6b4484bef902a59f3fa66e33b\",\n      \"obligation_ids\": [\n        \"C-forwarded-context\"\n      ],\n      \"binding_ids\": [\n        \"BD-forwarded-context\"\n      ],\n      \"relation_ids\": [],\n      \"scope\": {\n        \"description\": \"Per-status correlation through completed forwarded-read response routing in a crash-free three-full-voter cluster with current-term committed history and distinct request contexts.\",\n        \"assumptions\": [\n          \"Each originating follower has one outstanding operation in the checked history, allowing independent correlation by origin.\",\n          \"All actual protocol messages are delivered without mutation; the overlap delays earlier heartbeat probes until later-context confirmation has completed.\",\n          \"Peer caller persists each update before message delivery and applies bootstrap configuration/no-op entries in order.\"\n        ],\n        \"excluded\": [\n          \"No claim of a client API deadline, infinite stall, state-machine read linearizability violation, or crash durability failure.\",\n          \"No membership changes, observer/witness roles, snapshots, or term changes during the read phase.\"\n        ],\n        \"parameters\": {}\n      },\n      \"rationale\": \"Ground the selected status-consumption responsibility without assuming a violation or any unconditional client deadline.\",\n      \"status\": \"pending\",\n      \"previous_id\": null,\n      \"version\": 1,\n      \"boundary_changes\": [],\n      \"obligation_checks\": {},\n      \"remaining_obligation_ids\": [\n        \"C-forwarded-context\"\n      ],\n      \"recheck_reasons\": [],\n      \"coverage_limitations\": [\n        \"Direct check b21be9de584f4ca6b5964cbf24384304 is incomplete: Direct oracle correspondence is unreviewed; Nonzero direct test exit (test_failure); inspect raw stack and target path before attribution; Correlated prerequisites not established: No corresponding prerequisite events reached: admitted/read_admitted; No applicable completed result event was reached\"\n      ],\n      \"progress\": [\n        {\n          \"claim_id\": \"C-forwarded-context\",\n          \"artifact_id\": \"b21be9de584f4ca6b5964cbf24384304\",\n          \"check_id\": \"957fd78098304be69986dc2a90daee5c\",\n          \"record_status\": \"execution_incomplete\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"record\": {\n        \"path\": \"state.json\",\n        \"collection\": \